What is the max lenght for a int date:

AI Overview
The maximum value an int can hold in Java is 2,147,483,647. 
Because int represents a numerical value and not a sequence, it does not have a "length" in terms of characters or elements. Instead, it has a strict size constraint defined by the Oracle Java Specification: 
Key Specifications

    Maximum Value: 2,147,483,647 (accessible via Integer.MAX_VALUE)
    Minimum Value: -2,147,483,648 (accessible via Integer.MIN_VALUE)
    Max Digit Length: 10 digits (when formatted as a positive string)
    Memory Size: 32 bits (4 bytes) 

Related Maximum Lengths in Java
If you meant the maximum length of Java data structures that use an int for indexing: 

    Arrays: The theoretical maximum capacity of a Java array is 2,147,483,647 elements.
    Strings: The maximum character length of a String is 2,147,483,647 characters. 

What happens if you exceed it?
If you add 1 to Integer.MAX_VALUE, Java will not throw an error by default. Instead, it wraps around to the minimum negative value (-2,147,483,648) due to integer overflow. 
If you need to store whole numbers larger than 2.14 billion, use the long data type or the BigInteger class. 
